WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000 align:start position:0% line:0%
Transcriber: Maki Sugimoto 

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:05.335
Sometimes citizens think,

00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:08.964
“Oh, this is my personal problem
or a personal issue.

00:00:09.422 --> 00:00:13.802
So it’s kind of a waste
of time to speak up.”

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:15.136
But this is not true.

00:00:15.512 --> 00:00:20.850
If someone speaks up
and others agree with it,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.646
that personal issue
becomes social issue.

00:00:25.021 --> 00:00:26.940
With my administration,

00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:30.902
the city government actually
did not make a town vision.

00:00:31.778 --> 00:00:37.033
Instead of that, citizens
created the vision by themselves

00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:42.038
and we, local government,
supported the process,

00:00:42.038 --> 00:00:44.874
because [a] city is citizens --

00:00:46.251 --> 00:00:48.545
[a] city is not the government.

00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:51.464
I am Takashima Ryosuke,

00:00:51.506 --> 00:00:53.508
the youngest mayor in Japanese history.

00:00:54.092 --> 00:00:56.052
I’m the mayor of Ashiya City.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.347
(Speaking in Japanese)

00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:02.934
I’m a mayor, but I’m not a politician.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:06.563
My stance is actually very simple.

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:10.817
I just listen to
as many voices as possible,

00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:12.777
especially (from) younger generations.

00:01:12.777 --> 00:01:14.613
The reason is very simple:

00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:18.199
students under 18 cannot vote.

00:01:19.034 --> 00:01:20.744
So I visited schools,

00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:23.246
like junior high schools
and elementary schools,

00:01:23.288 --> 00:01:25.290
to hear their voices.

00:01:25.332 --> 00:01:31.046
But it’s so hard for kids, for students,
to speak their opinions to a mayor --

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:33.381
even if I am the youngest mayor.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.302
So what I did was eat
school lunch together,

00:01:40.096 --> 00:01:44.267
and I repeatedly visited schools.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.896
I didn’t want to be a formal visit,

00:01:47.937 --> 00:01:49.939
but rather a casual visit,

00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:53.234
casual chat with teachers and students.

00:01:54.027 --> 00:01:58.114
I could create the kind
of friendly atmosphere,

00:01:58.114 --> 00:02:02.869
and I got more information
rather than [in] a formal visit.

00:02:03.244 --> 00:02:08.958
For example, some students told me
their school gym was so hot.

00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:13.713
So we decided to install air conditioners

00:02:13.755 --> 00:02:16.049
in every single school gym.

00:02:16.966 --> 00:02:21.805
I wanted to make schools a place
to learn and practice democracy.

00:02:22.222 --> 00:02:25.392
And it's all about
communication and dialogue.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:31.648
I wanted to encourage people
to speak up, listen to their voices,

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.401
and then reflect their voices.

00:02:34.442 --> 00:02:38.363
The main method is holding
dialogue meetings.

00:02:38.655 --> 00:02:42.992
It’s a meeting with me,
mayor, and citizens

00:02:43.034 --> 00:02:46.162
sit down together in a circle
and talk with each other.

00:02:46.621 --> 00:02:51.167
And sometimes the mayor
does not even speak up.

00:02:51.543 --> 00:02:56.923
Just listens or facilitates
what citizens want to talk about.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:02.137
So, for example,
Ashiya is a very healthy city.

00:03:02.178 --> 00:03:07.434
Recently, we had the world's
oldest person in Ashiya city.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:11.771
Around 30 percent of the citizens
are over 65.

00:03:11.813 --> 00:03:13.022
In the dialogue meetings,

00:03:13.064 --> 00:03:17.485
I heard elderly people say
that the community centers were too busy

00:03:17.485 --> 00:03:19.904
to answer their questions about care.

00:03:20.363 --> 00:03:24.075
So I wanted to increase
the number of community centers,

00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:26.202
but we needed some budget.

00:03:26.244 --> 00:03:28.788
So before we had a monetary gift
for elderly people,

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.459
so we decided to change
our monetary gift system,

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.043
from a one-time monetary gift

00:03:34.085 --> 00:03:36.838
to creating [a] new community center

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.549
where elderly people and their families

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:41.926
get some advice on wellness.

00:03:42.802 --> 00:03:46.431
Some people say monetary gifts
are a kind of symbol of respect.

00:03:47.348 --> 00:03:48.975
So some people argued

00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:52.979
that I had no respect for elderly people.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.190
But through the dialogue sessions,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.443
I explained why this was important

00:03:58.485 --> 00:04:03.114
and why this actually
benefited for elderly people.

00:04:04.115 --> 00:04:08.578
And I also cut my future monetary gift.

00:04:09.162 --> 00:04:12.665
So this was not like others’ problem;

00:04:12.707 --> 00:04:14.334
this was our problem.

00:04:14.876 --> 00:04:18.546
Finally, they (came to) understand
why we needed to change.

00:04:19.047 --> 00:04:25.178
They changed their opinion
because they understood the process.

00:04:26.221 --> 00:04:30.517
During cherry blossom season,
when cherry blossoms bloom beautifully,

00:04:30.558 --> 00:04:34.062
local shops wanted to close the street

00:04:34.062 --> 00:04:38.024
to enjoy food
under the cherry blossoms.

00:04:38.024 --> 00:04:41.986
But for local residents,
that proposal was simply inconvenient,

00:04:42.362 --> 00:04:43.947
so it was controversial.

00:04:44.781 --> 00:04:51.371
But when local citizens and local shops
actually joined the process

00:04:51.412 --> 00:04:54.749
and citizens proposed the plan,

00:04:54.749 --> 00:04:57.001
the proposal was a success.

00:04:57.585 --> 00:05:02.131
So citizens actually
created the vision of (our) town,

00:05:02.173 --> 00:05:03.508
not the government.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.052
People tend to think

00:05:06.094 --> 00:05:09.848
that the ones who make society better
are the government

00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:11.808
or someone else.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.351
and not ourselves.

00:05:13.935 --> 00:05:16.145
I want to change that mindset.

00:05:16.604 --> 00:05:18.231
It is everyone.

00:05:18.565 --> 00:05:21.943
It's every single person
who can make society better

00:05:21.985 --> 00:05:24.988
and who can contribute
to making society better.

00:05:24.988 --> 00:05:26.656
That is what I want to do.

00:05:30.368 --> 00:05:31.578
Thank you.

